---
import BrandName from './BrandName.astro';
---

<section class="mission-section" aria-labelledby="mission-title">
  <div class="section-shell mission-layout">
    <div class="mission-heading" data-reveal>
      <p class="section-kicker">Why <BrandName /></p>
      <h2 id="mission-title">Genetic knowledge should serve everyone.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mission-copy" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
      <p class="mission-copy__lead">
        Human genetic variation—the differences in DNA found among people and
        populations—influences disease, diagnosis, medicines, and discovery. Yet
        much of what the world has measured remains scattered across
        publications and databases, difficult to compare, and unevenly
        representative of the people it is meant to benefit.
      </p>
      <p>
        <BrandName /> is building a shared atlas that brings this evidence together
        across geography and biological scale. The goal is not simply to make another
        database. It is to turn fragmented knowledge into an accessible resource that
        helps researchers, health programmes, and the public ask better questions—and
        makes missing knowledge impossible to overlook.
      </p>
      <p>
        Location matters because a genetic variant can be common in one
        population and rare in another. Geography describes the evidence
        collected from populations; it does not predict any individual person’s
        genome.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-shell community-panel" data-reveal>
    <div class="community-panel__copy">
      <p class="section-kicker">Built in the open</p>
      <h3>A global community can build what no single lab can.</h3>
      <p>
        <BrandName /> is open source and being developed for the public good. Contributors
        around the world can add local knowledge, find overlooked evidence, improve
        the models, shape the interface, and challenge the project’s assumptions.
        Decisions and progress stay visible on GitHub.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="community-actions" aria-label="Join genomeOS on GitHub">
      <a
        class="github-cta github-cta--primary"
        href="https://github.com/genomeOS/genomeOS/discussions/76"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <span>Meet the community</span>
        <strong>Introduce yourself</strong>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="github-cta"
        href="https://github.com/genomeOS/genomeOS/issues"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <span>Explore the work</span>
        <strong>Browse GitHub Issues</strong>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="github-cta"
        href="https://github.com/orgs/genomeOS/projects/1"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <span>See the roadmap</span>
        <strong>Open the project board</strong>
        <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
